---
import LandingLayout from '@/layouts/LandingLayout.astro';
import { project } from '@/config/project.config';
import { withBase } from '@/lib/base';
import '@/styles/project.css';
---

<LandingLayout title="Privacy" description={`How ${project.name} handles your data.`}>
  <main id="main-content" class="project-site doc-page">
    <div class="project-shell">
      <article>
        <div class="section-kicker">PRIVACY POLICY</div>
        <h1>Privacy</h1>
        <p>{project.name} connects only to the Feishin server address you enter. It has no accounts, analytics, advertising or tracking, and it sends nothing to the developer or any third party.</p>

        <h2>What the app stores</h2>
        <p>The app stores saved server addresses, usernames and theme choices in its private app storage. Passwords are stored separately using Android Keystore encryption. Deleting a saved server removes its password, and uninstalling the app removes everything it stored. Android cloud backup is turned off for the app.</p>

        <h2>Network connections</h2>
        <p>Feishin serves Remote over plain HTTP by default. Credentials and playback data sent that way can be seen by other devices on an untrusted network, so use a trusted network or an HTTPS/WSS connection you control. See <a href={withBase('/docs/security/')}>Security</a> for details.</p>

        <h2>This website</h2>
        <p>This site shows screenshots and a video of the app. It sets no cookies and uses no analytics. Its hosting provider may collect information needed to serve the site, such as IP addresses in server logs.</p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>Questions about privacy can be raised as an issue in the <a href={project.repository}>source repository</a>.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </main>
</LandingLayout>
